            <ArticleTitle>Mycobacterium orygis Lymphadenitis in New York, USA.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1749-1751</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2310.170490</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of lymphadenitis caused by Mycobacterium orygis in an immunocompetent person in Stony Brook, New York, USA. Initial real-time PCR assay failed to provide a final subspecies identification within the M. tuberculosis complex, but whole-genome sequencing characterized the isolate as M. orygis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
